Recommends: homelab-api
Description: Centralized background-job engine for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Executes long-running work submitted by any other homelab-* feature over
 HTTP, fronted by homelab-api's /api/v1/jobs/* gateway route the same way
 homelab-mailbridge backs /api/v1/mail/*. Zip-building is the first job
 type; the engine itself is generic (a small Perl module-per-type
 interface, see README.md) so future types -- SHA1 hashing, image
 resizing, video transcoding, full-account bundling -- are additive, not
 a rewrite. Deliberately host-independent: output artifacts live on this
 host's own disk, never assumed to share a filesystem with whatever
 feature submitted the job. Job state lives entirely in Postgres, so a
 crash or restart at any point recovers cleanly via an automatic
 stale-job reclaim sweep, not in-process memory.
